GAL22V10
TILEGLUE

BCLK  BLATCH RLATCH TW  BFIRST TDATA LDATA BDATA NC   NC    NC   GND
NC    Q0     Q1     Q2  Q3     BW    TCLK  LCLK  LATCH NPL  DS   VCC

; --- bit counter ('161 in rev A/B), clocked by the board clock, cleared by the latch ---
Q0.R  = /Q0
Q1.R  = Q1 * /Q0 + /Q1 * Q0
Q2.R  = Q2 * /Q1 + Q2 * /Q0 + /Q2 * Q1 * Q0
Q3.R  = Q3 * /Q2 + Q3 * /Q1 + Q3 * /Q0 + /Q3 * Q2 * Q1 * Q0
Q0.E  = GND
Q1.E  = GND
Q2.E  = GND
Q3.E  = GND

; --- column-end flag ('74 + 2G08 + 2G32): sticky, set when the passing frame's last bit
;     (T_endcol of that tile) is 1 at the 16-bit boundary; drives B_W towards the tile below
BW.R  = BW + BDATA * Q0 * Q1 * Q2 * Q3

; --- clock towards the top (W = 0) or the left (W = 1), W = T_W * B_first ('125/'126) ---
; T_clk: the 22V10 output enable is a single product term and W = 0 needs an OR, so T_clk
; is driven low when not selected instead of floating (a falling edge at most: the
; registers count rising edges, so no spurious clock)
TCLK  = BCLK * /TW + BCLK * /BFIRST
LCLK.T = BCLK
LCLK.E = TW * BFIRST

; --- latch merge ('32 + '04): to the neighbours and, inverted, to the '165 /PL ---
LATCH = BLATCH + RLATCH
NPL   = /BLATCH * /RLATCH

; --- serial input of the '165 chain: from the left when W = 1, from the top otherwise ---
DS    = TW * BFIRST * LDATA + /TW * TDATA + /BFIRST * TDATA

; asynchronous reset of every register while the latch is high (AR is a single product
; term in the 22V10, so it uses the feedback of the LATCH output = B_latch + R_latch)
AR    = LATCH
SP    = GND

DESCRIPTION

Isomorphic keyboard tile, rev-A/B glue logic in one ATF22V10C.
Replaces U101 (2G126), U102 (2G08), U105 (1G04), U106 (2G32), U107 (2G125),
U108 (2G74) and U109 ('161). The two '165 shift registers stay.
Derived 1:1 from the rev-A netlist (hardware/kicad/tile). One deliberate difference:
T_clk is driven low instead of tri-stated when the chain turns left (W = 1).
